{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "BUmCsnLGGX8roz1u7",
	"notes": "A House Navigator: minor interstellar nobility born with the third eye, bred over millennia by the Navis Nobilite to survive and steer by it. Deliberately does not include Psyker (Talent), Unusual Background (Latent Psychic Potential), or Warp Empowerment — Navigators are not psykers drawing on the Thaumatology: Sorcery-modelled disciplines in Imperium/Traits/Psykers and the Warp.adq, they carry a single, fixed, inherited gift instead (the Third Eye carries no Warp Sorcery modifier and so is never gated by the spell-cost cap that governs sanctioned powers). Point math: 70 (attributes: IQ 40 + HT 10 + Will 20) + 22 (Navigator's Third Eye: Warp Sight 13 + Lethal Gaze 9) + 10 (Status 2) + 20 (Wealthy) - 5 (Distinctive Features) - 10 (Duty to House and Navis Nobilite) + 24 (skills) = 131 points before a GM adds age, House politics, or extra shipboard skills — a well-off specialist, not a line combatant, sitting between framework.md's \"Trained soldier\" and \"Elite human\" tiers. A GM running a Navigator across centuries of service should add escalating Unnatural Features levels as the character's own mutation-with-age (see the parent trait's lore note); this template leaves that as an open dial rather than a fixed cost.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
