		{
			"id": "tboEk9_3-m0-Pj14W",
			"name": "Duty (House Navigator / Navis Nobilite)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Quite often (12 or less). Bound by the Navis Nobilite's warrant and House obligations, and by contract to a vessel, Rogue Trader dynasty or House.\n\nLore: A Navigator is not a free agent: the Navis Nobilite's warrant licenses the House, and House Navigators are contracted to ships, Rogue Traders or the House itself, who call on their service far more often than not.\n\nDesign: Duty (B133), quite often (12 or less), -10, the same rate used for the Sanctioned Psyker's Duty to the Astra Telepathica.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Navis Nobilite"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "tMrQnx74bba2eKn73",
			"name": "Distinctive Features (Third Eye)",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Even bound shut, the brow ridge and scar tissue of the third eye mark a Navigator as visibly inhuman to anyone who looks closely.\n\nDesign: Basic's Distinctive Features (a fixed, minor -5 for a feature that is unusual but easily hidden under a wrap or hood).",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Navis Nobilite"
			],
			"base_points": -5
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "s_Kz4NSaywgXKjP8-",
			"name": "Navigation",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Navigation (Hyperspace) renamed and restricted per framework.md — the specific, trained skill of reading the third eye's sight into a safe course through the immaterium.\n\nDesign: 20 points in a Hard skill is IQ+4 before the Third Eye's bonus. A Navigator trains from childhood for this one job; a ship-rated Navigator should be the best in the galaxy at it, so this is weighted well above the template's other skills.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Psyker",
				"Navis Nobilite"
			],
			"specialization": "Warp",
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"points": 20
		},
